%N A398706 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} beta(k)/(k^2*(k+1)), where beta(n) = A206369(n) is the alternating sum of divisors of n.
%C A398706 This constant appears in the asymptotic formula for the function A398704(n)/A398705(n).
%H A398706 Jing Ma and Huayan Sun, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s11139-022-00588-y">On a sum involving certain arithmetic functions and the integral part function</a>, The Ramanujan Journal, Vol. 60, No. 4 (2023), pp. 1025-1032; <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s11139-026-01336-2">Correction</a>, ibid., Vol. 69 (2026); <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.02924">arXiv preprint</a>, arXiv:2109.02924 [math.NT], 2021; <a href="https://www.researchgate.net/publication/361229857">ResearchGate link</a>. See Theorem 1, p. 1027.
%F A398706 Equals 1/2 + Sum_{k>=3} (-1)^k * (D(k) - 1), where D(s) = zeta(s-1)*zeta(2*s)/zeta(s) is the Dirichlet g.f. of beta.
%e A398706 0.808426630713118864076053891398587918109774547661006...
%o A398706 (PARI) suminf(k = 3, (-1)^(k+1) * (zeta(k-1)*zeta(2*k)/zeta(k)  - 1)) + 1/2
%Y A398706 Cf. A206369, A398700, A398704, A398705.
